{"title":"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Rigorous,_but_straightforward)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Rigorous, but straightforward)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many ordered pairs of positive <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d65e341986740d4269b766b4d01bf615ded39061.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/b/66b3fe3c9678d2b8be2ef9cf5fbe183ebb78d11c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&lt;x\\le 100,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a95c5a2b8b4b599c61dcf363d82c688344ad56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd4dc1d53a29456a06ab2b08e589f2773f56578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+1}{y+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"44\" height=\"40\" /> integers?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/0/de079b6605b9963069d7ed01ce6096d75a16eae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y|x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/e/07e9ad6ba383441e1a79e0b8cb6a14aa0c34b020.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+1|x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/7/db79edf1bcc94de6ebbe969a9a63043d34d55805.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{gcd}\\,(y,x)=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> (the bars indicate <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility\" title=\"Divisibility\">divisibility</a>) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe891c0c9a38e525dfdb2169629dcfd30f19c267.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{gcd}\\,(y+1,x+1)=y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euclidean_algorithm\" title=\"Euclidean algorithm\">Euclidean algorithm</a>, these can be rewritten respectively as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45efc884581c363008b4fa60795b6c89e45a0caa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{gcd}\\,(y,x-y)=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/a/57abc5812c89b713417163454778d4151d342f8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{gcd}\\, (y+1,x-y)=y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />, which implies that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/c/94ce8cb856b55a2bef39e7a6d77e5a37baed5123.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,y+1 | x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />. Also, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/46279d326bdb262a1e50c414da8b258cd17db4c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{gcd}\\,(y,y+1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/15152b8074257e4c8200d48bcc57a25e24c6132c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y(y+1)|x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />. <sup><span id=\"ref_1\">[<a href=\"#note_1\">1</a>]</span></sup>\n</p><p>Thus, for a given value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we need the number of multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/417873bfdf96eefd3de26b6db28dc88c30f04d2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y(y+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c78f65261e1dfd9f03d4e9afd2580095aaa2063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/310cd110c1de9689172c645ddcb341c9b01cd55e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />, but not including 0 because x cannot be equal to y). It follows that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c18334e4ce8c366b36e6003dfc2f6e74f5466890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\frac{100-y}{y(y+1)} \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"85\" height=\"43\" /> satisfactory positive integers for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/6/ef6a049fc32fbe8b4b9058dad225115ca02a3868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\le 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />. The answer is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b08a1c5231be8c3d8b6b09431be4f2db16f701b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{y=1}^{99} \\left\\lfloor\\frac{100-y}{y(y+1)} \\right\\rfloor = 49 + 16 + 8 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 1 = \\boxed{085}.\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p><br /><br /><span id=\"note_1\"><a href=\"#ref_1\">^</a></span> Another way of stating this is to note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd4dc1d53a29456a06ab2b08e589f2773f56578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+1}{y+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"44\" height=\"40\" /> are integers, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/1/581e53a1b4eb9411afafb5428bc2fc85de74209f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y} - 1 = \\frac{x-y}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"114\" height=\"36\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/0/4906836b938fc0daeae49d5e92841f7ca43629f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+1}{y+1} - 1 = \\frac{x-y}{y+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"145\" height=\"40\" /> must be integers. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/8/7f801b9f0ef3c2c1d614cd42c8abd34ebedf7c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> cannot share common prime factors, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26e542d80fcae3fc42be85a118ed69a651246796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x-y}{y(y+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"67\" height=\"37\" /> must also be an integer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643bb188b64bc21cbfea1ef1d884ec740a1a4ed2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\equiv 0 \\mod y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/637fed4261c14e5d1360797150000f4ff74d1ae1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1 \\equiv 0 \\mod y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"168\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc396057fa790468d057dc505f6fc4ab973c58d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ky$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812f3604761edf45426216059143d1cd0d36a2d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ky+1 \\equiv 0\\mod y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"177\" height=\"16\" />. We can add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> to each side in order to factor out a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/8/7f801b9f0ef3c2c1d614cd42c8abd34ebedf7c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/4/9549821eeeeea8e58d2f8d5ba40e96fec239bf2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ky+k+1 \\equiv k \\mod y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"210\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f00642e24fb85e6735854e791f00c970c2f6c19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(y+1)+1 \\equiv k \\mod y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"223\" height=\"18\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/a/8fabf62a3bac92d0181abbda317e881093b6a546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(y+1) \\equiv 0 \\mod y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"18\" />. We finally achieve the congruence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5eda7e0ce661366ce29ef23abd7806fcf4b97488.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-k \\equiv 0 \\mod y+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>We can now write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb30a8dc04720b98c9d1c7ed937e49005033b63e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y+1)a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />. Plugging this back in, if we have a value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f8f512f05d06f29a7dd3b5e35129072d871952e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = ky = ((y+1)a+1)y = y(y+1)a+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"328\" height=\"18\" />. We only have to check values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f030dffc3302fd6e05146f5e8c201a9b543a3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y(y+1)&lt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />. This yields the equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/27836fd5e89f4935d9bfc6d3041132448874e8ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2a+1, 6a+2, 12a+3, 20a+4, 30a+5, 42a+6, 56a+7, 72a+8, 90a+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"612\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>Finding all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b519d4c9362313ac369ba9761878a4b326e8d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&lt;x&lt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c87aef85c91416e4f6e73582258fd6d882f21ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49 + 16 + 8 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 1 = \\boxed{085}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"344\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Rigorous.2C_but_straightforward.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Rigorous,_but_straightforward)\">Solution 3 (Rigorous, but straightforward)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Rigorous, but straightforward)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use casework: \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3b4834614e5e7e189cb7d621cfb4fb0bd36dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d57e864142ab75fd2c899a6c3ec5614aa4fe7e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,5,\\cdots ,99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> cases. \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40ac4b6f5ab516ac6fe7132ed2fe7a1d77ca02dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f59578a03fce082b9df9c32b22c1abe0f1befc4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8,14,\\cdots ,98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cases. \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b0e1404de4eca35c42876bcc83707b753e990e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da2aea54a54037d842a018737e48fed276600096.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15,27,\\cdots ,99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases. \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/b/45bc0006df273cb384b6c864236b3c1bf292e898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81cffdb31c5648a6c7c4634a92f7ec4e27542b69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24,44\\cdots ,84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases. \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd049e624a41c0df950b22dadf2257ee2ad9410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39d75485c8632354250f89d8849063e7a01fa641.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35,65,95$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases. \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daaf07d9f0a2413768e291d1264b59b3c835e4aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5a9ef6c34834316d183577aca699ee87f121b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48,90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cases. \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c37261466c0ff756401c32f293c33e111f4712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/8/848ec5b5f695afbacb864efead154761481780c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> case. \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/4/8a4808fab877e290bdc0e68ce61cc8a852fd397b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> case. \n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c1b3337268879246336b597a1b8d88b2f17019.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> case. \n</p><p>Adding, we get our final result of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f5725f8c460fe2f5bb0b76c47a23d5ae17988cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{085}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"45\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>Note: In general, all of the solutions for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b3e59f2e1b009ce5ebfd2008d4ae05574d85b22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+by(y+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" />, for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee43dad66edfcfbf0df826428070ae01b63ae10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+by(y+1)=x&lt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>~SirAppel\n</p><p>Also, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> just starts with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1634e096091d715474ea902e171593169de7130d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"21\" />, and adds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/417873bfdf96eefd3de26b6db28dc88c30f04d2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y(y+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> until it is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~Yiyj1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME\" title=\"1995 AIME\">1995 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1995 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1995\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1995 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017185049\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.073 seconds\n